  "theorem_statement": "Inside the native 480-element automorphism group of G60, the registered reconstruction packet and the complete sixty-state multiplier assignment each have stabilizer C2, but these are distinct subgroups with trivial intersection. The packet-preserving involution is exactly translation by the exported V4 deck element a. It fixes G15, G30, and all K6 point labels while reversing the multiplier value on the twenty states in the ten C23 fibers. The assignment-preserving involution fixes the multiplier assignment, root, C23 support, and C33 support, but moves both split-orientation blocks and sends exceptional point 0 to point 1. The two involutions commute, their product has order 2, and together they generate a Klein four subgroup. Their stabilizer intersection is the identity, so the packet and assignment jointly rigidify the registered decorated G60 structure.",
  "verdict": "multiplier_packet_and_full_assignment_have_crossed_c2_stabilizers_generating_v4"
}
